---
// Goal: list the ten built-in jq transforms and show how to run one, since thinkthen prints them and jq runs them.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import { TOOLS_SEE } from '../../data/reference.mjs';
import { captioned } from '../../data/samples.mjs';

const [list, show] = captioned('reference/transform', TOOLS_SEE.transform);
const spec = 'https://github.com/botassembly/thinkthen/blob/main/specification/transform.md';
const CATALOG = [
  ['band', 'How many answers a band settles, and how many of those are right.'],
  ['calibration', 'Whether answers given at a probability of 0.8 are right about eight times in ten.'],
  ['compare', 'What changed between two runs, and the likely cause.'],
  ['cost', 'The input tokens a run spent, and what they cost at your prices.'],
  ['counts', 'How many answers were yes, no, and not sure.'],
  ['monitor', 'How often each action of a policy ran, was reviewed, and was changed.'],
  ['score', 'How many answers are right at a cut, against your labels.'],
  ['sweep', 'What every cut would have done.'],
  ['triage', 'A policy: whether a support ticket is drafted, blocked, or reviewed, and why.'],
  ['trials', 'One row per record from repeated runs, before another transform reads them.'],
];
---
<Base title="transform" description={'The ten built-in jq transforms, and how to run one.'}>
  <h1><code>transform</code></h1>
  <p class="lede">ThinkThen ships ten <code>jq</code> programs that read saved runs. <code>thinkthen transform</code> prints them. It never runs one. <code>jq</code> does.</p>

  <h2 id="list">The catalog</h2>
  <Terminal run={list} caption={list.see} />
  <table>
    <tr><th>Transform</th><th>What it answers</th></tr>
    {CATALOG.map(([name, what]) => (<tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{what}</td></tr>))}
  </table>
  <p><code>band</code>, <code>score</code>, <code>sweep</code> and <code>trials</code> read a band as the commands do. A probability exactly at the band's low edge is not sure. The <a href="/functions/decide/#thresholds">decide reference</a> gives the rule.</p>

  <h2 id="show">Run one</h2>
  <p><code>thinkthen transform show NAME</code> prints one transform exactly as shipped. Save it, then hand it to <code>jq -f</code> with a saved run. Each transform's first lines say what it reads and what arguments it takes. An unknown name prints nothing and exits 2.</p>
  <Terminal run={show} caption={show.see} />

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/functions/audit/">audit</a> · <a href={spec}>The transform specification</a></p>
</Base>
